dates age v1
description "The day an age goes up, under the Act on Calculation of Age and Article 143 of the Civil Code: counted from the day of birth, the first day counted, a year ends on the day before the day that corresponds to the birthday, and on the last day of February for one born on 29 February in a year that has none. The reference's lines for the age"

inputs
  birth      : date  range >=2000-01-01 <=2010-12-31
  year_count : int   range >=1 <=20

date first_day = birth                          # counted from the day of birth: the first day counts
date last_day = first_day
  + year_count years else start_of_next_month   # the corresponding day; with none, the 1st of the month after
  - 1 day                                       # the day before it: the age goes up when this day ends

claims
  last_day_is_monotonic : last_day is monotonic
